              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Southwest Airlines, section\u202f1 of the Federal Arbitration Act exempts only classes of workers that work on an instrumentality of foreign or interstate commerce, such as a plane, ship, or train, as it moves goods or people across borders."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Southwest",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "2ddef3554d3b7430bceec138581bb714ad46b67b2df3695672b091edc6e7f720",
              "evidence_ids": [
